jira:PROJ750
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "750" ;
    jira:title "POWL v2 Recursive Workflow Sockets & Parent-Child Closure Geometry" ;
    jira:section "A" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently double-verified this session.** `SocketPath`/`SocketKind`/`WorkflowSocketId`/`Powl::sockets()`/`Powl::socket_at()`/`ParentChildEdge`/`ParentChildClosure` in `crates/powl2-decompose/src/powl.rs` — additive structures (not new tree-node variants, a deliberate choice to avoid breaking existing exhaustive matches) computed over the existing `Powl` tree via deterministic DFS (`BTreeSet`/`BTreeMap` only). 15 new tests + 4 pre-existing external-cut tests + 7 decompose tests, all passing; clippy/fmt clean. **Corrected this session (adversarial review)**: \"determinism-checked (3x identical runs)\" was OVERCLAIMED as stated — only `Powl::sockets()` has a real double-computation-and-compare test; `ParentChildClosure`'s determinism is asserted in a doc comment only, never exercised by a test. \"Zero downstream breakage in the sole in-workspace dependent\" was also inaccurate — `praxis-core` was a dependent too (via dev-dependencies) at the time of the claim. Test depth is shallow: no 3+-level nesting, no cyclic `ChoiceGraph`, no nested `ExternalCut` case is covered. Gap: still zero downstream consumers (not wired into `decompose.rs`/`recompose.rs`/`powl_projection.rs` emission) — structurally sound, not yet used. **Remediation this session (agent `ab7087992bb3b26b4`) — ALIVE, Cargo-verified.** New `three_level_nested_model()` fixture (`≺(≺(γ(a, b), c), d)`, `SocketPath` depth 3 — deeper than any existing fixture) and `parent_child_closure_is_deterministic_across_calls_three_level_nesting`, computing `parent_child_closure()` twice and asserting full equality (all 3 internal fields via derived `PartialEq`, strictly more coverage than `sockets_is_deterministic_across_calls`'s flat-set comparison). `just powl2-decompose-test`: 20 unit tests + 7 integration tests, 0 failed. The remaining \"zero downstream consumers\" and \"no cyclic/nested-ExternalCut coverage\" gaps are real but out of this remediation's narrow scope (determinism claim only) — left open as known, disclosed library-maturity gaps, not defects." .

jira:PROJ751
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "751" ;
    jira:title "External Cut Admission Wiring & SPARQL Projection (Q) Vocabulary Alignment" ;
    jira:section "A" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ750 ;
    jira:evidence "**Adversarially reviewed this session — one real, previously-undisclosed gap found, corrected here.** `admit_powl_model()` recursively gating every `ExternalCut` node before `powl_to_turtle` emits RDF is confirmed real (exhaustive over all 4 `Powl` variants, first statement in `powl_to_turtle`, no caller bypasses it). Real SPARQL execution via `run_render_model_projection()` confirmed genuine (real oxigraph store, exact-value assertions, not `.is_ok()`). **Corrected claim**: \"full overlap, zero leftover mismatch\" between `render_model_projection.rq` and the emitter was independently re-checked and is FALSE query→emitter — the emitter's `Powl::Choice` arm emits 8 real predicates (`powl2:startNode`/`endNode`/`hasNode`/`ofChildIndex`/`edgeSource`/`edgeTarget`/`hasEdge`, plus root `derivedFrom`) that appear NOWHERE in `render_model_projection.rq`. Any POWL model containing a `Choice` (XOR/loop routing) node has its entire routing topology silently dropped from the SPARQL projection — no error, zero test coverage of a `Choice` node through the query. This is real silent data loss requiring remediation: extend the query to cover the `Choice` predicate set, add a test with a `Choice`-containing model asserting the routing edges survive projection. **Remediation this session (agent `a08726afdad5d2e3b`) — ALIVE, independently regression-tested.** Extended `render_model_projection.rq` with 8 new SELECT variables + matching `OPTIONAL` blocks covering the full `Choice` predicate set, and `ProjectionRow`/`run_render_model_projection` in `powl_projection.rs` to populate them. New test `admitted_choice_node_produces_real_sparql_routing_projection_rows` builds a real 2-child XOR model and asserts every routing node/edge/`ofChildIndex` with exact values. Cargo-level test execution was BLOCKED by the (now-being-fixed) external `wasm4pm-compat` issue, so the agent independently validated the query itself with `rdflib` (not the crate's real oxigraph engine, but a genuine independent SPARQL implementation): parsed clean, produced exactly the predicted rows against a hand-built fixture mirroring the real emitter's output, and confirmed the pre-existing non-Choice projection path is byte-identical before/after (11 rows, same bindings) — a real regression check, not just a new-path check. Self-disclosed process deviation: the agent ran one bare `cargo check` directly before catching itself and switching to `just`-only — flagged honestly rather than omitted. **Live-verified after the wasm4pm-compat fix (see environmental note at end of file)**: `just praxis-graphlaw-test-lib \"test(admitted_choice_node_produces_real_sparql_routing_projection_rows)\"` → `PASS`, `1 test run: 1 passed`." .

jira:PROJ752
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "752" ;
    jira:title "Tera Renderer (T) & Real Projection Receipt for Receipted Arazzo" ;
    jira:section "A" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ751 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently double-verified this session.** Real `tera` dependency (reused, already pinned elsewhere in the workspace) + `crates/praxis-core/templates/arazzo_projection.tera`, rendering PROJ-751's real `ProjectionRow`s into a genuine Arazzo 1.1.0 JSON document. `ArazzoProjectionReceipt::from_materials()` computes all four digest fields as real BLAKE3 hashes of the real Turtle/query/template/output bytes (independently re-verified by recomputing the hashes outside the constructor and asserting equality — not just \"a hash exists\"). Round-trip test proves the rendered document parses via `wasm4pm-arazzo`'s own real Arazzo admission (`DocumentIndex::add_document`), not a hand-built fixture. A real bug (duplicate `rdf:type` triples double-counting children) was found and fixed during this build. `air_digest_hex` was honestly left caller-supplied pending PROJ-753 rather than faked — and once PROJ-753 landed later in the same session, the placeholder sentinel was replaced with a real digest. Gap: not yet called from any production runtime path." .

jira:PROJ753
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "753" ;
    jira:title "Arazzo→AIR Lowering Bridge" ;
    jira:section "B" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ752 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently double-verified this session — the load-bearing gap for all of Rail B is closed.** `crates/wasm4pm-arazzo/src/lower.rs` (new) is the first real function anywhere in the repo lowering a genuinely parsed `ArazzoDescription` into `AirProgram`: step identity, parameter/body expressions, outputs, and a new `AirRouting`/`AirRoutingOutcome` type pair for success/failure routing (End/Retry/GotoStep/GotoWorkflow), including local component-reference dereferencing. Routing content is folded into the canonical BLAKE3 digest and WASM custom section (proven by a test showing the digest changes when routing is stripped, not silently dropped). End-to-end proof at two levels: a hand-written realistic Arazzo document taken through the complete real `parse → resolve → lower → normalize → compile_to_wasm` chain, asserting 7 distinctive source-document strings survive into the compiled WASM bytes; and PROJ-752's own manufactured document extended through the same full chain. **Corrected this session (adversarial review, independently re-checked)**: the claim that 4 disclosed out-of-scope gaps are \"refused rather than fabricated\" is OVERCLAIMED — true for only 1 of 4. Cross-document component references genuinely fire a typed `Refusal`. The other 3 — parameter `$ref` dereferencing, `RequestBody.replacements`, workflow-level (not step-level) routing — are silently skipped/never read with no error surfaced at all, a direct violation of this repo's own Invariant #1 (\"no silent defaults — every error is a typed Refusal\"). Remediation: either add a typed `Refusal` for each of the 3 silent-skip paths, or narrow the parser to reject documents using those constructs outright rather than accepting-and-discarding them. **PROJ-810 (\"refusal is not the default\" build wave) — ALIVE, adversarially re-verified independently this session, not just claimed.** All 3 silent-skip paths above now have real end-to-end implementations, narrowing refusal to only genuinely-invalid input: `resolve_parameter_reference` (`lower.rs:892`) genuinely dereferences `#/components/parameters/<name>` against `Components.parameters`, wired into `lower_step`. `apply_payload_replacements` (`lower.rs:950`) uses real `serde_json::Value::pointer_mut` in declaration order; the 3 remaining refusal boundaries (xpath/other selector, dangling pointer, no-payload) were independently confirmed genuinely irreducible — no evaluator exists in this crate for those cases, not an excuse. `merge_success_actions`/`merge_failure_actions` (`lower.rs:708,731`) implement real override-by-name-preserve-order-else logic, wired through `lower_workflow`→`lower_step`. `cargo test -p wasm4pm-arazzo` (full suite): 55 lib + 8 e2e + others, 0 failed — independently re-run by the adversarial verifier, not just cited. `cargo fmt`/`clippy -D warnings` clean; no panics/unwraps outside `#[cfg(test)]`. **Remediation this session (agent `a5a4ed05a4dde41f5`) — ALIVE (source), Cargo-level test run BLOCKED at the time by the external wasm4pm-compat issue (now being fixed separately).** New `Refusal::UnsupportedFeature(String)` variant, wired into all 3 previously-silent paths: parameter `$ref` now refuses instead of being skipped, non-empty `RequestBody.replacements` now refuses instead of never being read, non-empty workflow-level `success_actions`/`failure_actions` now refuse before any step lowers. 4 new negative tests, one per construct. In lieu of a compiler run (blocked): brace-balance checked all 3 touched files, ran standalone `rustfmt --check` against the full module tree (zero diff), and grepped repo-wide for any exhaustive `match` on `Refusal` the new variant could break (none — the only external consumer stores it as formatted text). Combined in the same agent with PROJ-784's remediation (same crate, avoiding a file-scope collision) — see PROJ-784 below. **Live-verified after the wasm4pm-compat fix**: `just wasm4pm-arazzo-test` → all 4 new negative tests (`refuses_step_parameter_that_is_a_reference`, `refuses_request_body_with_replacements`, `refuses_workflow_level_success_actions`, `refuses_workflow_level_failure_actions`) pass, full suite 47 passed/0 failed." .

jira:PROJ754
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "754" ;
    jira:title "Typed Refusal Taxonomy for the Arazzo→AIR Compiler" ;
    jira:section "B" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ753 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently double-verified this session.** 3 new `Refusal` variants (`CyclicStepDependency` via iterative DFS over `depends_on`, `UnsupportedCriterion` for non-simple criterion shapes, `MalformedRetryPolicy` for invalid timeout/retry fields), each wired into real previously-unchecked lowering-time constructs with dedicated tests (13 new). \"Missing operationId\" and \"unresolvable reference\" were deliberately mapped onto the pre-existing `MissingIdentity`/`UnresolvableReference` variants rather than duplicated — documented as a judgment call, not silently reused. Capstone end-to-end test: a real JSON document with an intentional dangling-dependency defect goes through the complete real pipeline and the specific typed refusal fires, naming both the dangling and offending step ids. **Adversarially reviewed this session**: real, minor coverage gaps — `CyclicStepDependency` is only tested for 1-2 node cycles, no 3+-node cycle case; `MalformedRetryPolicy` is only unit-tested, no end-to-end JSON-driven proof it's reachable from a real document. Lower-severity than PROJ-751/753's findings — the variants themselves are real and correctly triggered where tested, this is a coverage gap not a correctness defect. **Remediation this session (agent `a1a58cb691e214e5d`) — ALIVE, Cargo-verified.** Added `refuses_three_step_cyclic_dependency` (3-node cycle A→B→C→A, hand-traced then confirmed empirically that the DFS closes the cycle at step_a) and `malformed_retry_policy_is_refused_end_to_end_through_the_real_pipeline` (real JSON document, `retryLimit: 0`, taken through the complete `parse → resolve → lower` chain, asserting the refusal names both the offending action and the actual invalid value). `just wasm4pm-arazzo-test`: unit tests 48 passed (was 47), `end_to_end_lowering.rs` 8 passed (was 7), 0 failed. No production code touched — additive tests only." .

jira:PROJ755
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "755" ;
    jira:title "AIR Transition Core: Correct δ_AIR Signature & Remove Direct I/O" ;
    jira:section "C" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ750 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ751 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ752 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ753 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ754 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** `air_core:transition/2` now returns `{context(), [command()]}` per PRD §7.7's `δ_AIR:(S,E)→(S',C)` (`C` = newly-ready-step dispatch commands, computed via `NextMask band (bnot Mask1)` so an already-active step sharing a predecessor isn't re-issued a command). Direct I/O (`dispatch_http`/`dispatch_rdma`) confirmed already absent repo-wide; only the one real, needed NIF (`eval_expr_nif`) remains. All 3 real callers (`arazzo_runner_workflow.erl`, `arazzo_atomvm_workflow.erl`, `fortune5_test.erl`) updated to the new 2-tuple shape. `rebar3 compile` exit 0, `rebar3 eunit` 6/6 passing. Added `apps/air_core/src/air_core.app.src` (previously absent — required for `rebar3` to compile the app at all; overlaps PROJ-756's umbrella item, disclosed not hidden)." .

jira:PROJ756
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "756" ;
    jira:title "AIR Transition Core: AND/Join Readiness & Deterministic Corpus" ;
    jira:section "C" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ755 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** Real multi-predecessor AND/join semantics: `#context{}` gained a static `pred_mask_map` (inverted `next` edges, built once in `new/1`) and a cumulative `completed_mask`; a successor is only newly-ready when *every* predecessor bit is in `completed_mask`, not on the first one (the prior OR-semantics bug `fortune5_test.erl`'s own comment admitted faking around). Proved via a new 4-node diamond test (D depends on B+C, both depend on A) and by deleting `fortune5_test.erl`'s manual `set_active_steps` workaround entirely — `dispatch_freight` now becomes ready through the real transition logic once both real predecessors complete. Root `rebar.config` added (none existed anywhere in the repo); `rebar3 compile`/`eunit` now run from repo root, 9-10 tests (harness double-count quirk, 0 failures every time, confirmed 3x). Deterministic golden-digest corpus: `air_core_corpus_test.erl`, 6-step workflow with an AND-join and an interleaved `step_failed`, canonicalized via `term_to_binary`, hashed with the real `b3sum` CLI (not a new NIF, to stay within just-only cargo discipline), golden digest `7277d8a08de8a936103a8baaa65244dcc8676fed8cf857634bb70ff55e508829` reconfirmed across 4 separate process invocations." .

jira:PROJ757
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "757" ;
    jira:title "OTP Runner: Workflow Identity, Reaction Events & Restart-from-Replay" ;
    jira:section "D" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ755 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ756 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** Design decision: extended `apps/arazzo_runner/` in place rather than rebuilding the deleted `apps/otp_runner/` (PRD §7.7 names exactly two wrappers, \"OTP and AtomVM\" — a third app has no home in the PRD's layering; justified in a header comment). New `#workflow_identity{}` (10 PRD fields) + DETS-backed durable persistence (`arazzo_runner_identity.erl`); all 9 reaction-event classes wired with genuine state changes; `restart => temporary` → `transient` (justified against `permanent`, which would fight a normally-finished or admission-refused workflow). Real, non-simulated crash-restart proof: actual `exit(Pid, kill)` + supervisor-driven restart, identity and `air_core` progress confirmed unchanged under the new PID. Found and fixed forward 2 real pre-existing bugs surfaced by being the first tests to actually exercise `start_link`: the `pg` scope was never started anywhere in the supervision tree (every io_worker crashed on first message); the infra bootstrap loop had no failure-detection (intermittent hang, reproduced via a 300-iteration kill/restart stress script — ~1-in-5 to 1-in-10 before the fix, 0-in-300 after). `rebar3 compile`/`eunit` — 12/12 passing (10 pre-existing air_core + 3 new), re-run 10+ times, always 0 failures. Disclosed PARTIAL: `dispatch_ready`/`acknowledgment`/`admission_result` are correctly handled but only reachable via direct event injection today — PROJ-758 (the broker) doesn't exist yet, same honesty pattern as PROJ-755/756's `Commands`." .

jira:PROJ758
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "758" ;
    jira:title "Broker Dispatch, Correlation & Return-Admission Path" ;
    jira:section "D" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ755 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ757 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** New `arazzo_runner_broker.erl` inside `apps/arazzo_runner/` (design decision: broker gates the existing io-worker pool it's named after, not a new app — PRD names exactly two transition-core wrappers, not a tenth layer). Real pre-actuation verification + post-actuation obligations (PRD §13): genuine idempotency dedup proven via evidence-chain-head equality on repeat dispatch, sha256 evidence chain genuinely extending per-workflow. Real return-admission chain (PRD §8, 6-stage pipeline): correlation + authority stages hard-enforced via a one-shot minted token; provenance/structure/semantic stages explicitly marked `?UNENFORCED_RETURN_STAGES` for PROJ-785, not silently assumed. `DIRECT_ACTUATION_REFUSED` enforced mechanically, not documentarily — `enqueue_io/2` now requires an atomically-consumed (`ets:take/2`, no TOCTOU) broker-minted token; proven via bogus-token and token-reuse negative tests. **Corrected this session (adversarial review)**: \"only 3 of 9 pre-actuation checks are enforceable today, the other 6 have no Erlang-side data source\" is OVERCLAIMED for at least 1 of those 6 — `required_prior_receipts` has a real data source available today: `receipt_head` already exists on the `#workflow_identity{}` record (PROJ-757) at the same depth of effort as the 3 checks this ticket did implement. This should be reclassified from \"no data source\" to \"not yet wired,\" and implemented rather than left in the unenforced set. Found and fixed a real DETS table-name collision bug (first ticket to add a second DETS-using test module alongside PROJ-757's). Test count corrected: \"23/23 `rebar3 eunit` tests\" is actually 22 distinct tests — a harness double-count inflated the reported total by 1. 5 consecutive determinism runs. Disclosed: sha256 (not BLAKE3) for this Erlang-side ledger — explicitly not claiming Rust receipt-discipline compliance since no Rust code is touched; dispatch is synchronous/inline, not a decoupled async dispatcher. Correctly left PROJ-785's 5 remaining refusal codes (`BROKER_RECEIPT_PRECONDITION_MISSING`, `CORRELATION_MISMATCH`, `RETURN_PROVENANCE_MISSING`, `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED`, `RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED`) untouched rather than guessing at them. Idempotency proof itself independently re-verified as genuinely strong. **Most severe production defect of the whole session, found and fixed this session — PARTIAL, personally re-verified, one disclosed regression still being fixed.** A Fortune-5 audit found `admit_return/3` had zero production callers anywhere in `apps/*/src/` — a dispatched step's captured result never flowed back into `air_core:transition`, so a workflow that genuinely succeeded permanently stalled waiting for a result event that never arrived. Fixed: `do_dispatch_actuate/6` now calls `admit_return/3` (real correlation_id + return_authority_token, the same dispatch's own real minted values) immediately after recording actuation, handling all 3 outcomes explicitly (admitted / genuine refusal propagated / workflow-not-found leaves the entry `actuated` rather than falsely failing a real actuation). **Personally re-verified, not just trusted**: ran `rebar3 eunit --module=arazzo_runner_broker_test` myself (17/17, clean, no filter tricks), and specifically confirmed `test_full_dispatch_correlation_return_round_trip` (its own docstring: \"the return-admission loop closes ON ITS OWN, with no direct admit_return/3 call anywhere in this test\") is real and passing. Two more real, severe defects fixed in the same pass: **unsalted authority tokens** (`dispatch_token`/`actuation_token`/`return_authority_token` were SHA-256 of public identifiers alone, forgeable by anyone who knew workflow/step IDs) — now mixed with a real per-node secret (`crypto:strong_rand_bytes/1`, `persistent_term`, race-safe), proven with a negative test computing tokens the old unsalted way and confirming both `enqueue_io/2` and `admit_return/3` now reject them. **TOCTOU race in idempotency dedup** — the separate lookup+insert became a single atomic `ets:insert_new`, proven with a real concurrency test (two processes on a synchronization barrier), run 10x by the builder and independently spot-checked, 0 failures. **Disclosed regression — now closed, ALIVE, full suite green.** Correctly fixing the return-path changed real observable behavior 3 pre-existing tests had encoded as if the old broken behavior were permanent. Root cause precisely diagnosed, not papered over: a broker-dispatched step with `{literal, ...}` outputs derives an empty `required_result_types` set, which the echo worker's generic response vacuously satisfies — so the step auto-admitted and self-completed the instant it became ready, desynchronizing fixtures that assumed steps stayed inert. Fix used an already-existing PROJ-785 gate (not a new mechanism): gave every broker-dispatched step a real typed output binding (`{op, 'and', {var, '__result__'}, {literal, true}}`), so `admit_return/3` now deterministically refuses the echo worker's auto-dispatch via the real `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED` gate, and only the tests' own explicit reaction/corpus events genuinely admit a step — the 3 fixtures now assert this refusal explicitly rather than relying on timing. Golden digests recomputed from real `b3sum` output, not hand-derived; the differential harness's `EXPECTED_COMMAND_TRAIL`/`refusal_class` needed no changes (reasoned through first, then confirmed by the real run). No assertions weakened. **Personally re-verified independently, 3 consecutive runs**: `rebar3 eunit` → 55 tests, 0 failures, every run. This ticket, and the 3 severe defects fixed alongside it (auth token forgery, TOCTOU dedup race), are now fully closed with no open regression. **Remediation this session (agent `a09d097892f1082b9`) — ALIVE, fully verified.** `required_prior_receipts` implemented as `check_required_prior_receipts/5` in `arazzo_runner_broker.erl`, chained into `dispatch/4` right after the existing correlation gate; refuses `BROKER_RECEIPT_PRECONDITION_MISSING` (already named in PRD §18) when `receipt_head` is not a non-empty binary, before any ledger entry/token is minted. Removed from `?UNENFORCED_PREACTUATION_CHECKS` (now 5 unenforced, not 6). 2 new tests added (`test_broker_receipt_precondition_missing_on_dispatch` negative, `test_required_prior_receipts_present_proceeds` positive), both driven through a real `air_core` transition. Full suite: `rebar3 eunit` run 7 consecutive times, `25 tests, 0 failures` every time. `rebar3 compile` clean. This closes PROJ-785's `BROKER_RECEIPT_PRECONDITION_MISSING` too — see PROJ-785 note below." .

jira:PROJ759
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "759" ;
    jira:title "Parent-Child Closure & Compensation-as-Workflow" ;
    jira:section "D" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ757 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ758 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** New `crates/praxis-graphlaw/src/chatman/closure.rs`/`closure_test.rs`: `RecursiveSocketClosure` built directly on `powl2-decompose`'s existing `WorkflowSocketId`/`ParentChildClosure` machinery (PROJ-750/751, correctly reused not duplicated). Real, tested `all_required` (`Close(W) iff forall c in C(W), TerminalAdmitted(c)`) and `quorum(q)`, exactly the PRD's formulas. Three-state `ChildCompletionState` (`Open`/`Observed`/`Admitted`) implements PRD §9's \"a child completion signal SHALL be treated as observation until admitted\" — a merely-`Observed` child correctly refuses `ChildCompletionUnadmitted`. PRD Scenarios §19.4/§19.5 implemented as literal executable tests. The other 4 named closure kinds (`any_sufficient`/`ordered_subset`/`policy_decides`/`first_conformant`) are established as real `ClosureLaw` catalog variants but correctly refuse `ClosureLawNotImplemented` rather than faking semantics — explicitly PROJ-773's scope. New `crates/praxis-graphlaw/src/chatman/compensation.rs`/`compensation_test.rs`: `manufacture_compensation_workflow` is the sole constructor of `CompensationWorkflow`/`CompensationDispatch` — grep-confirmed zero `rollback()` function exists anywhere in the module. Every PRD §10 element (authority, admitted inputs, expected consequence, dispatch, receipt, replay) validated non-empty with an independent refusal test. `CompensationLedger` enforces append-only at the API surface (only `append`, no `remove`/`clear`/`pop`). Receipts reuse the existing `abi::Receipt`/BLAKE3 machinery, no new hash scheme; determinism is itself a tested property. 6 new `Refusal` variants, each with a real triggering test, deliberately not yet added to the cross-lane catalog (`ALL_REFUSAL_NAMES`) — that's PROJ-786's scope, matching the PROJ-779/780/783 precedent. 30 new tests (19 closure + 11 compensation), `just chatman-verify`: 131 passed/923 skipped, `chatman_static_gates` 11/11, atlas verification PASS, 5 consecutive determinism runs identical. Clean concurrency hygiene: re-read `abi.rs` fresh before editing since other concurrent agents (PROJ-780/783-area) had it open, made only tail-appending edits, did not touch `engine.rs`/`powl_projection.rs`/`router.rs`/`powl2-decompose` at all. Honest, disclosed deferrals: the 4 unimplemented closure kinds (PROJ-773), the observation→admission promotion gate itself (PROJ-774), the 7-kind compensation catalog (PROJ-776), wiring compensation into `ChatmanEngine`'s sealed S1-S6 pipeline (materially larger than this ticket's \"establish the manufacture-path skeleton\" scope, and `engine.rs` had a live concurrent editor), and full PRD §18 catalog wiring (PROJ-786). This lands the foundation that unblocks PROJ-772/773/774/775/776 for future work." .

jira:PROJ760
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "760" ;
    jira:title "AtomVM Wrapper — Execute AIR Transition Semantics" ;
    jira:section "E" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ755 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ756 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ757 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** Resolved as a thin delegation facade (`atomvm_runner.erl` → `arazzo_atomvm_workflow.erl`) rather than a duplicate implementation, per PRD §7.9's \"SHALL NOT maintain a separate semantic implementation.\" Found and fixed a real bug during verification: `start/1` probed nonexistent `air_core:initial_state/0`, so every workflow started with `undefined` core state and crashed on its first event (reproduced live before fixing). Added the missing `atomvm_runner.app.src` build entrypoint; `rebar3 compile` now picks up all 4 apps. 15/15 `rebar3 eunit` tests, run 3× for determinism. Disclosed: no AtomVM runtime is installed in this environment — verification is real logic-level proof via plain BEAM/OTP, not a live AtomVM target; that remains correctly out-of-scope future work. `PROOF_OF_EQUIVALENCE.md` updated to point at PROJ-761 as the real evidence surface going forward." .

jira:PROJ761
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "761" ;
    jira:title "OTP/AtomVM Differential Conformance Corpus" ;
    jira:section "E" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ760 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** New `apps/arazzo_runner/test/arazzo_runner_atomvm_differential_test.erl`: a 6-event ordered corpus (linear segment, AND-join, one genuine timeout failure — the 3 shapes the task required) driven identically through both the OTP path (real `arazzo_runner_workflow` + broker, valid identity so it actually actuates) and the AtomVM path (`arazzo_atomvm_workflow` directly, matching PROJ-760's honest scoping — no live AtomVM runtime in this environment). Command sequence, the one dimension AtomVM doesn't natively expose (it computes but discards `air_core`'s `Commands`, per its own existing code comment), was captured via standard BEAM call tracing (`erlang:trace/3`, not a NIF) rather than modifying either wrapper's source. All 4 PRD §7.9 dimensions (state digest, result digest, refusal class, command sequence) confirmed byte-identical between OTP and AtomVM for this corpus — golden digests pinned in the test file. Genuine, disclosed finding: this is an exposure asymmetry (OTP routes through a persistent broker audit trail, AtomVM discards the same computed command), not a semantic divergence — cross-checked against OTP's own native `broker_dispatches` trail so tracing isn't the sole witness. `rebar3 eunit`: 31 tests, 0 failures, 7 consecutive runs byte-identical. Correctly handled a real concurrent-edit collision with the PROJ-785 agent (same `apps/arazzo_runner/`) by polling until it stabilized rather than touching the contested files. Disclosed scope: one corpus (6 events), not an exhaustive AIR-program equivalence proof — the event translator only covers `result`/`timeout` reaction classes, fails loud (not silently) on anything else." .

jira:PROJ762
    a jira:Ticket ;
