    jira:evidence "**Built this session — ALIVE, adversarially re-verified.** `observe/2`/`compare_four_dimensions/2`/`first_mismatch/1` (`apps/arazzo_runner/test/arazzo_runner_atomvm_differential_test.erl`) extract the 4-dimension comparison into the `{refused, Code, Details}` idiom already established by `arazzo_runner_broker.erl`. Negative fixture (`test_semantic_drift_refusal_fires_on_correct_dimension`) sends AtomVM one extra `finalize` beyond the shared corpus and confirms `command_trail` — checked first, per documented priority — is correctly reported as the diverging dimension. `rebar3 eunit --module=arazzo_runner_atomvm_differential_test`: 4/4, independently re-run twice. Full suite: 34/0." .

jira:PROJ763
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "763" ;
    jira:title "OTLP→RDF Admission Mapper (closes gap G11)" ;
    jira:section "F" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** `crates/cng/src/otel_rdf.rs`: in-process re-validation of the same 5-attribute `event.praxis.activity_executed` contract Weaver's live registry check validates externally (that external gate, `just otel-weaver-live`, was real and untouched — this closes the separate gap of admitting spans not round-tripped through it), refusing via new typed `CngRefusal::OtelSpanRefused` (`CNG_R27`) before any triple is produced. Ungated `telemetry_gen` (previously `otel-live`-feature-gated) since it has zero external deps, keeping the mapper in the crate's default build surface — verified `otel-live` still builds after the change. RDF projection reuses real OCEL 2.0 vocabulary with zero unnecessary minting (`ocel:objectId`/`objectTypeName`/`hasObjectType`/`relatesTo`/`hasAttribute`); only 2 bridge-minted properties + 7 raw-OTLP properties with no OCEL/PROV-O equivalent. 10 new tests (specific-triple assertions + determinism proof, byte-identical across runs and independent of attribute order); `just cng-test-lib`/`cng-test` (default features, no bench/otel-live) both fully green, proving the mapper works in the truly default build. Found and fixed a real pre-existing bug along the way: invalid Turtle syntax (Rust-style backslash line-continuation misused inside a Turtle string literal) in `otel-bridge.ttl`, caught by a test that parses the file. **Adversarially reviewed this session**: the admission mapper and its math are genuinely solid, but it is reachable ONLY from its own unit tests — zero production callers anywhere in the workspace (confirmed by grep). A real integration gap, not a defect; the actual fix is PROJ-764's job (rewire the OCEL CONSTRUCT queries to call this mapper from a real pipeline entry point). **Resolved by PROJ-764 (below) this session** — the mapper is now called from a real `G_OTEL` → `G_OCEL` CONSTRUCT projection pipeline, not just its own tests." .

jira:PROJ764
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "764" ;
    jira:title "Rewire OCEL CONSTRUCT queries onto admitted evidence + 5-layer graph separation" ;
    jira:section "F" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ763 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** No existing \"OTel→OCEL\" CONSTRUCT query actually existed to re-point — the pre-existing `ocel-*.construct.rq` files are the unrelated RWAI benchmark's own `obs:`-vocabulary pipeline, structurally incompatible with `urn:graph:otel`'s real shape — so a new, dedicated CONSTRUCT query (`queries/otel-to-ocel.construct.rq`) was built matching the handoff doc's literal `G_OCEL = CONSTRUCT_P(G_OTEL)` equation. New module `crates/cng/src/otel_ocel.rs`: real 5-layer named-graph separation (`G_SOURCE`/`G_OTEL`/`G_OCEL`/`G_RESULT`/`G_RECEIPT`) — confirmed genuine, not aliased, by a test proving each graph is independently queryable with distinct content. New `CngRefusal::OcelConstructRefused` (`CNG_R28`). 8 new tests: exact-triple assertions, determinism (byte-identical across 2 runs, order-independent), empty-input and malformed-Turtle negative cases, genuine-separation proof. Verified PROJ-763's own disclosed scope note against the handoff doc's literal text (not a paraphrase) before proceeding, confirming this ticket's imperative-mapper reuse doesn't violate the forbidden-alternatives clause. Found and fixed 2 real oxigraph 0.5.9 bugs along the way: `xsd:dateTime + xsd:dayTimeDuration` silently drops solutions for multi-year durations (worked around via Howard Hinnant's `civil_from_days` integer arithmetic instead), and a chained `A - B - C` numeric expression mis-associates as `A - (B <op> C)` instead of left-associative — fixed by splitting into single-operator `BIND` steps, documented with 2 independently-verified reference dates. `just cng-check`/`cng-test-lib` (124 passed)/`cng-test`/`cng-test-bench` all exit 0, 0 failed. Honest, disclosed gap: `G_RESULT`/`G_RECEIPT` are real, distinct, reserved graphs but deliberately left unpopulated — their content is PROJ-765's (PROV-O ancestry/receipt) and PROJ-766's (Rail F evidence) explicit scope; populating them here would preempt that work." .

jira:PROJ765
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "765" ;
    jira:title "PROV-O transformation ancestry + CONSTRUCT provenance receipt" ;
    jira:section "F" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ763 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ764 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** New `crates/cng/src/otel_receipt.rs`: `receipt_otel_to_ocel` computes the handoff doc's 3 constitutional digests (`digest(P) + digest(G_OTEL) -> digest(G_OCEL)` — CONSTRUCT query text, `G_OTEL`'s canonical content, `G_OCEL`'s canonical content obtained by actually calling `otel_ocel::project_otel_to_ocel`, never caller-supplied) and folds them into one `cngr:receiptHead` via this crate's existing ordered-BLAKE3-hasher chain idiom. Real PROV-O ancestry written into `G_RECEIPT` (`prov:Activity`/`prov:Entity`/`prov:Plan`, reusing the crate's existing `prov:` prefix binding, no new one invented), content-addressed as `urn:blake3:<hex>` matching the crate's existing scheme. 7 new tests: independent digest-chain recomputation outside the function, exclusive `G_RECEIPT` placement, pure-function/no-mutation proof, determinism, graceful empty-graph handling. Reused `CngRefusal::OcelConstructRefused` with 2 new documented stage names rather than a redundant new variant — disclosed explicitly, not silently overloaded. `just cng-test`: 0 failed. **Reachability gap closed this session** — the whole `otel_rdf → otel_ocel → otel_receipt` chain had zero non-test callers. New `crates/cng/src/bin/otel-rdf-demo.rs` (`just cng-otel-rdf-demo`) wires one real fixture span through the full chain (`admit` → `project_admitted_spans`/`admitted_spans_to_trig` → `project_otel_to_ocel` → `receipt_otel_to_ocel` + `verify_receipt_otel_to_ocel`) using only already-tested `pub fn`s, printing the real receipt head and a full TriG dump. Real output: 21 `G_OCEL` quads, 15 `G_RECEIPT` quads, receipt independently verified, `RECEIPT_HEAD` deterministic and byte-identical across 2 separate runs. Post-change grep confirms all 5 chain functions now have a real non-test caller. `cargo test -p cng --lib otel_rdf_test otel_ocel_test otel_receipt_test`: 28/28, 0 regressions. Clippy clean on the new file." .

jira:PROJ766
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "766" ;
    jira:title "Multifractal measurement profile & execution measure μ_x" ;
    jira:section "G" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ764 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** New `crates/cng/src/measurement.rs`: real SPARQL SELECT execution measure (`mu_x`, PRD §14) over `G_OCEL`. Scope resolved directly against the PRD text: this ticket is the raw measurement-profile schema + `mu_x` itself, NOT PROJ-767's `Z(q,ε)/τ(q)/D(q)/f(α)` statistics (untouched, still `pub(super)`-scoped) — wiring the estimator onto this module's output is named as a distinct, not-yet-scoped follow-up, not silently implied done. Of the 11 PRD-named `DeclaredProcessScale` variants, exactly 2 (`Workflow`, `Activity`) have a real data source in `G_OCEL` today; the other 9 correctly refuse new `CngRefusal::MeasurementEvidenceInsufficient` (`CNG_R29`) rather than fabricating a zero — matches Rail G's anti-relabeling mandate this session established for PROJ-767. Raw integer `mass` only in the receipted graph (no float in canonical paths); `source_ocel_digest` computed via a real shared digest helper, never asserted. 11 new tests covering grouping, evidence-threshold refusal, empty-graph refusal, exclusive `G_RESULT` placement, determinism. Self-caught and fixed forward a real mid-session issue: `lib.rs` was found reset to its pre-PROJ-763/764 state partway through (a stale formatter-hook mtime effect, not a competing agent, confirmed via `git show HEAD`) — re-applied full module wiring, verified correct by fresh read plus a green `cng-check`/`cng-test-lib`/`cng-test`. `just cng-test-lib --features bench`: 142 passed, 0 failed; `just cng-test`: 0 failed; refusal-variant coverage extended to 29 (`CNG_R01..CNG_R29`). **Extended this session (PROJ-810 build wave) — ALIVE, adversarially re-verified.** A 3rd `DeclaredProcessScale` (`ObjectCentricAggregationLevel`) now has a real data source, built end-to-end through the actual `admissible_span()` → `project_admitted_spans` → `project_otel_to_ocel` pipeline (not hand-built OCEL) — verifier independently confirmed `Order`/`Payment` masses of 1 each via a real query against real projected data. `process.object.type` confirmed `required` in the OTLP attribute contract. The remaining 8 refusals are each individually confirmed distinct and genuine (`each_of_the_eight_no_data_scales_refuses_with_a_distinct_scale_specific_reason`, re-run, passes). `cargo test -p cng --lib measurement::`: 13/13, independently re-run." .

jira:PROJ767
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "767" ;
    jira:title "Z(q,ε)/τ(q)/α/f(α) estimator + explicit measurement standing" ;
    jira:section "G" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ766 ;
    jira:evidence "**Estimator built and independently verified this session (Track 2b of `../RAIL_G_MEASUREMENT_DESIGN.md`).** `crates/cng/src/bench/multifractal.rs`: real `Z(q,epsilon)`/`tau(q)`/`D(q)`/`f(alpha)` via log-log regression + Legendre transform, proven against a binomial cascade with an independently-known closed-form `tau(q)` (matched <1e-8) and a monofractal negative control (13 tests, `cargo test -p cng --features bench --lib multifractal_test`, all pass; `just cng-test-bench` 172 tests pass, no regressions). Run against one real 64-tick workday: `D(q)` measured flat at 1.0 (monofractal), root-caused to the benchmark corpus generator emitting a fixed 8 ops/set regardless of category — an honest negative result per this ticket's own anti-relabeling mandate, not a false `MULTIFRACTAL_ADMITTED`. New typed refusal `CngRefusal::MultifractalFitDegenerate` (`CNG_R26`) for degenerate fits (<2 scales, zero-variance input, etc.), wired through the crate's exhaustive-match test pattern. Gap: the explicit standing-status *enum* (as opposed to the anti-relabeling behavior, which is already correct in practice) is not yet a separate typed artifact; module is `pub(super)`-scoped to `cng`'s `bench` module, not yet a public API for Track 1 or external callers. **Adversarially reviewed this session, including the adjacent PDDL temporal-planner wiring that feeds Rail G's temporal tape** (`bcinr_pddl::GroundTemporalProblem::find_temporal_plan` + `powl_bridge::temporal_plan_to_powl_tape`, `engine.rs:1159-1222`/`powl_projection.rs:76-174`): the \"2, not 3\" causal-edge fixture result is confirmed mathematically correct by independent hand computation, and a 300,000-trial brute-force model check (Python transcription of both real functions) found the transitive-closure recovery algorithm exact — but only under an undocumented, unenforced precondition (`steps` sorted by non-decreasing `start_time`). The one real producer (`find_temporal_plan`) guarantees this by construction, but `TemporalPlan`/`TemporalPlanStep` are `pub` with a `pub steps: Vec<...>` field, and the test suite's own pattern of direct construction (bypassing the real planner) is an established, supported pattern — so a directly-constructed, out-of-order `TemporalPlan` can silently drop a required precedence edge with no `Refusal`, no error. Real, precisely locatable gap (missing precondition doc/assertion in `project_temporal_plan_to_powl`'s public contract), not reachable via the one real production producer today. Separately confirmed (self-disclosed, not concealed): `plan_temporal_tape_for_snapshot` has zero production callers anywhere in the workspace — its own doc comment already says so (\"read-only side-door... does not alter S3\"). Fortune-5 DoD: add either a debug-assert or a typed refusal enforcing the sort precondition before the recovery algorithm runs, so a future non-planner caller (e.g. a hand-constructed fixture, or a different scheduler) can't silently corrupt the recovered order. **Remediation this session (agent `aac0e3055ec5796b4`) — ALIVE, Cargo-verified.** Added an O(n) pre-check at the top of `project_temporal_plan_to_powl` (`plan.steps.windows(2)`, before the recovery algorithm runs) that refuses with the existing `Refusal::ValidationFailed` variant — an exact semantic fit, no new variant needed — if any step's `start_time` precedes its predecessor's. New test `out_of_order_temporal_plan_refuses_validation_failed` directly constructs an out-of-order plan and confirms it's now refused rather than silently corrupted. `just test-bin chatman_pddl_to_powl_temporal_concurrency`: 6 passed, 0 failed (all pre-existing real-planner tests plus the new one). Doc comments updated with the precondition and its O(n) cost. **Additional demonstration this session (agent `a54bebe6eea2fe1fc`): a real ART-shaped cross-story DAG proven through the full PDDL→POWL→closure-law chain — plus a real, previously undisclosed structural gap found in the process.** New `crates/praxis-graphlaw/tests/pddl_to_powl/art-cross-story-dag-snapshot.ttl` + `chatman_pddl_to_powl_art_dag_cross_story.rs` (5 tests): a shared story (`auth-migration`) gates two independent, unequal-duration features (`checkout-v2`/`admin-portal`) plus a third fully-independent feature (`reporting-dashboard`), converging at an `integration-milestone`. Real computed values matched hand-traced predictions exactly: shared/independent starts at t=0, gated features at t=4, milestone at t=9=`max(9,6,6)`. The projected `PartialOrder` forms a genuine diamond (6 pairs, `auth-migration` reaching the milestone via 2 distinct paths — a shape no strict tree can express), independently confirmed via `RecursiveSocketClosure` with real `AllRequired`/`Quorum(2)`/`AnySufficient` admission (both positive and negative cases). **Real gap found, honestly disclosed, not silently worked around**: `project_temporal_plan_to_powl` always returns a *flat* `PartialOrder` (every step a sibling of one root; the DAG lives entirely in that node's precedence `order` set), but `ParentChildClosure::from_model` (`powl2-decompose/src/powl.rs:402-459`) only ever walks tree *containment* (`children`/`region`), never a `PartialOrder`'s `order` relation — so there is today no direct wiring from a temporal-plan-projected precedence DAG to a closure-law socket's declared children. The demonstration worked around this by hand-building a separate nested `Powl` model reusing the real projector's leaf-label identities, not by silently patching over the gap. `just praxis-graphlaw-check-libtests`: clean. 2 pre-existing, unrelated clippy/test issues confirmed via `git status` to predate this change, correctly not attributed to it." .

