    jira:evidence "**PARTIAL, real progress this session**: (1) confirmed `lean`/`lake` resolve and work via `~/.elan/bin` (`crates/praxis-lean/src/lean.rs` already has this baked in as the default command path — real, not aspirational). (2) Ran `lake build` for real against the pre-existing `tools/paper-factory/lean-lake` corpus (not v26.7.11-authored, predates this milestone) — succeeded, 826 jobs, exit 0. (3) Ran `praxis-lean`'s own `no_sorry` audit against that corpus for the first time — found 71 unauthorized `axiom` declarations under its strict default policy (zero `sorry`/`admit`); some look like standard, legitimate cryptographic assumptions (e.g. collision-resistance) that formal proofs routinely axiomatize, not obvious shortcuts, but that distinction hasn't been made per-axiom yet. Added `crates/praxis-lean/tests/rail_h_existing_corpus_audit.rs` as a regression guard on this count (2/2 passing) so it can't silently grow. Still open: justfile wiring, and this ticket's original \"scaffold a NEW Rail H corpus\" framing was reconsidered — reusing the existing working Lake package via `Praxis/Corpus/`-style new files (PROJ-769's job) is more disciplined than duplicating package setup." .

