jira:PROJ771
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "771" ;
    jira:title "Process Cell Isolation & No-Shared-State Enforcement" ;
    jira:section "§8 (`PRD.md:460-474`)" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ757 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ758 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session.** `ChatmanEngine` (`crates/praxis-graphlaw/src/chatman/engine.rs:490-496`) has exactly 5 fields, all private, no `static`/`lazy_static`/`OnceCell`/`OnceLock`/`thread_local`/`Mutex`/`RwLock`/`Arc`/`Rc`/`RefCell`/`Cell` anywhere in `crates/praxis-graphlaw/src/chatman/` (repo-wide grep, confirmed) — both constructors build a fresh, private `oxigraph::store::Store` per instance, no cross-instance accessor exists in the public API. New test `process_cell_isolation_engine_b_cannot_observe_engine_a` (`engine_test.rs`): admits a full S1-S6 transition with a distinctive marker in engine A, proves engine B refuses `Refusal::SnapshotNotFound` when queried against A's snapshot id, then has B admit its own unmarked snapshot under the same id and confirms B's digests contain none of A's marker and differ from A's. Self-caught a test bug along the way (an over-strong assertion that digest #4 must always differ was removed after correctly failing — both engines legitimately derive the same OWL RL closure from the same RDFS fragment, not an isolation violation). Applying this session's PROJ-777/778 skepticism, also investigated `registry.rs`/`encoding.rs`'s disclosed process-wide statics (`LIST_REGISTRY`/`FORMULA_REGISTRY`/`GLOBAL_ENCODER`) for cross-instance leakage: real, pre-existing, already-disclosed coupling, but traced and confirmed NOT reachable through `ChatmanEngine`'s sealed public API (never accepts/returns a raw term id, `TripleStore`, or `Encoder`) — real debt, correctly left out of this narrow ticket's scope rather than attempting an unreviewed crate-wide refactor. `just praxis-graphlaw-test-lib \"test(process_cell_isolation)\"`: 1/1 pass; `test(chatman::engine)`: 17/17 pass. `cargo fmt --check` clean. Clippy BLOCKED by ~60 pre-existing errors confirmed unrelated to the touched file (zero hits in `engine_test.rs`/`engine.rs`)." .

