    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ753 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ756 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built this session — ALIVE.** Correctly scoped to `apps/arazzo_runner/` (PRD §7.8/§13, OTP runtime), not the Rust admission engine — a distinct concept from PROJ-752's compile-time `ArazzoProjectionReceipt` and this session's other receipt fixes. New `#event_receipt{}` (`arazzo_event_receipt.hrl`): all 10 PRD fields verbatim + a derived chain-head digest. New `arazzo_runner_blake3.erl`: real production BLAKE3 via `b3sum` (independently verified against published test vectors), typed `{ok,_}|{error,_}`, not `erlang:error`. New `arazzo_runner_event_receipt.erl`: `build/1` (real content-sensitive per-field digests) + `emit/1` (real ETS-backed chain-head pointer seeded from the existing `workflow_identity.receipt_head`, monotonic logic-tick clock, append-only log). Wired into one real production site: `arazzo_runner_broker.erl`'s `do_dispatch/6` now mints a receipt before any ledger entry or I/O, refusing outright if minting fails — closes a disclaimer that specific function already carried (\"not a substitute for... BLAKE3 canonical-N-Quads receipt discipline... out of this ticket's scope\"). All 15 pre-existing broker tests pass byte-for-byte unmodified (old `do_dispatch/6` body extracted unchanged into `do_dispatch_actuate/6`), proving no regression. 19 new tests (missing-field refusal, content-sensitivity, determinism, real end-to-end chain extension through a live workflow process). `just erlang-test`: 53/0; new modules run 3x: 19/19 every time. Disclosed, not hidden: only 1 of the 4 conceptual emission sites is wired (step-dispatching); step-completing (via consequence capture and via return-admission) and reaction-firing are named as deferred follow-up, deliberately not touched since `arazzo_runner_workflow.erl` had a live concurrent editor this session. PROJ-782 (replay verifier) is the next real consumer, correctly not built here." .

jira:PROJ782
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "782" ;
    jira:title "Replay Verifier: 5-Step Algorithm + Mismatch-Is-Refusal" ;
    jira:section "§15 (`PRD.md:717-726`)" ;
    jira:status jira:Blocked ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ781 ;
    jira:evidence "Implement replay exactly as specified: resolve AIR artifact by digest → restore admitted initial state → apply admitted ordered event corpus → recompute state/command digests → verify receipt-head equivalence. \"Replay mismatch SHALL be a typed refusal or build failure; it SHALL NOT be logged and ignored\" — this last clause is the one most often silently violated in practice; add a test that a deliberately corrupted receipt chain actually fails loud, not just logs a warning." .

jira:PROJ783
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "783" ;
    jira:title "Typed Refusal Catalog: Admission & Authority (10 codes — ticket title says 9, the list has 10, flagged not silently resolved)" ;
    jira:section "§18 (`PRD.md:845-858`)" ;
    jira:status jira:Partial ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ750 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ751 ;
    jira:evidence "**7/10 built and independently verified this session; 3/10 honestly BLOCKED, not faked.** ALIVE with real e2e triggers (not mocked): `POWL_REGION_NOT_ADMITTED`/`EXTERNAL_CUT_UNDECLARED` (upgraded from a generic `ValidationFailed` wrapper that was already firing under the wrong variant), `EXTERNAL_CUT_TYPE_MISMATCH` (new `resolve_external_cut_at`, first-ever caller of `powl2-decompose`'s previously-unused `SocketPath`/`socket_at`), `EXTERNAL_CUT_AUTHORITY_MISMATCH` (new cross-tenant IRI-authority check), `ARAZZO_UNMANUFACTURED`/`ARAZZO_SOURCE_RECEIPT_MISSING`/`ARAZZO_PROJECTION_DIGEST_MISMATCH` (new `admit_manufactured_arazzo`, tested against genuine Rail A/B pipeline output, not hand-typed fixtures). BLOCKED, correctly not fabricated: `RAW_OBSERVATION_NOT_ADMITTED` (Rail F doesn't exist; the closest analog already refuses correctly under a different variant, no gap to fix even if in scope), `BOUNDED_DESCENT_NOT_PROVEN` (PRD §6.6's cost-vector substitution law has zero implementation anywhere, confirmed by grep), `AMBIENT_AUTHORITY_REFUSED` (the one real non-fabricated trigger point is out of file scope this cycle; explicitly declined to add a syntax-based check since PRD §7.1 forbids inferring ambient authority from syntax). 9 new e2e tests across 2 new capstone test files. Coordinated file-scope with the concurrent PROJ-779 agent (same precedent for deferring shared-array/schema wiring). Clippy gate UNVERIFIED at session end — traced to a confirmed external cause (a concurrent process actively mutating the sibling `/Users/sac/wasm4pm-compat` checkout, unrelated to this diff), not claimed as passing. **Re-investigated this session (PROJ-810 build wave, now with Rail F real) — all 3 BLOCKED codes reconfirmed genuinely BLOCKED with fresh evidence, not stale.** `RAW_OBSERVATION_NOT_ADMITTED`: confirmed zero dependency edge between `crates/cng` and `crates/praxis-core` in either direction — Rail F (now real) and this crate are genuinely separate systems, no gap to close. `BOUNDED_DESCENT_NOT_PROVEN`: fresh repo-wide grep still finds exactly one hit (a catalog name only); `N3CostBound` confirmed a single-dimension counter, correctly distinguished from the PRD's 4D cost vector. `AMBIENT_AUTHORITY_REFUSED`: `authority_for()` confirmed still a name-only lookup; PRD §7.1's syntax-inference prohibition still correctly respected. No code changed — investigation-only, confirmed by re-run of `praxis-core-test` (clean)." .

jira:PROJ784
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "784" ;
    jira:title "Typed Refusal Catalog: AIR (4 codes)" ;
    jira:section "§18 (`PRD.md:854-857`)" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ753 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ754 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session, scoped entirely to `crates/wasm4pm-arazzo/`.** 3 of 4 codes turned out to already exist under different names (`AIR_REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED`→`Refusal::UnresolvableReference`, `AIR_CRITERION_UNSUPPORTED`→`Refusal::UnsupportedCriterion`, `AIR_PARSE_REFUSED`→`Refusal::Parse`) — documented as an explicit taxonomy-mapping doc block in `lib.rs` rather than renamed (10+ call sites, needless churn per API-stability discipline), with missing end-to-end pipeline coverage added for each. The 4th, `AIR_EXPRESSION_UNSUPPORTED`, was genuinely new and surfaced a real, previously-silent bug: `lower::lower_step`'s output-lowering loop read only the *keys* of `Step.outputs`, never the *value* — a `Selector`-shaped output was silently accepted with its shape discarded, the same class of gap PROJ-754 closed for criteria but missed on the output side. New `Refusal::UnsupportedExpression` + `classify_output_value` (mirrors `classify_criterion`) close it. `just wasm4pm-arazzo-test` (41 lib + 6 end-to-end, up from 4) and `-clippy` clean, run twice for stability; `just praxis-core-check` confirms the in-repo dependent crate is unaffected. **Adversarially reviewed this session — one real, previously-undisclosed correctness gap found, not in this ticket's own 4 codes but in a load-bearing neighbor.** `validate_step_dependencies` (PROJ-754, `lower.rs:163-220`, pure graph DFS over `depends_on`, order-agnostic) and `ReferenceResolver::resolve` (`temporal.rs:23-58`, a strict single left-to-right scan over raw JSON declaration order) implement two different, unreconciled notions of valid step ordering in the same pipeline — `lower_workflow` never reorders `AirWorkflow.steps` by the validated dependency graph. Concrete failure: a document where step_A is declared *first* with `dependsOn: [\"step_B\"]` (step_B declared second, and step_A's payload references `$steps.step_B.outputs.thing`) — a legitimate use of `depends_on` to declare non-textual execution order, exactly what the field exists for — passes `validate_step_dependencies` (acyclic, referentially sound) and lowers successfully, then gets wrongly refused by `ArazzoNormalizer::normalize` as `UnresolvableReference`, because the reference resolver assumes declaration order = dependency order. Grepped every `docs/jira/v26.7.11/*.md` for \"declaration order\"/\"depends_on\"/\"execution order\" — no acknowledgment of this specific divergence exists anywhere. Real, reachable gap for any document that uses `depends_on` non-textually combined with cross-step output references. Also: `compile_to_wasm`'s determinism claim is logically sound by static read (pure function, ordered iteration, BLAKE3, no RNG/wall-time/`HashMap`) but could not be empirically re-executed this session — `wasm4pm-compat` (the only dependency) is mid-refactor by a concurrent external process and does not currently build (`cargo check -p wasm4pm-arazzo` fails on `wasm4pm-compat = \"^26.6.29\"` vs. on-disk `26.6.5`, plus 14 unresolved-import errors inside `wasm4pm-compat` itself from an in-progress `wasm4pm-core` extraction) — downgraded from ALIVE to PARTIAL pending a live re-run once that sibling repo stabilizes. Minor: `src/vars.rs` and `src/bump_tree.rs` are dead, orphaned files — never referenced by any `mod` statement anywhere in the crate. **Remediation this session (agent `a5a4ed05a4dde41f5`, combined with PROJ-753) — ALIVE (source).** New `topological_sort_step_indices` (Kahn's algorithm, `BinaryHeap<Reverse<usize>>` ready-set, ties broken by original declaration index — no `HashMap` iteration ever determines order, preserving this repo's determinism invariant) in `lower.rs`; `lower_workflow` now sorts `AirWorkflow.steps` by the validated `depends_on` graph before the reference resolver runs, instead of raw source order. 2 new unit tests plus a full parse→resolve→lower→normalize capstone reproducing the ticket's exact forward-reference-via-`depends_on` scenario. Hand-traced for overflow safety (dep-count decrements are bounded by prior increments per edge) and confirmed a zero-dependency workflow provably reduces to original order. `temporal.rs`'s existing tests were deliberately left untouched (they build `AirProgram` by hand, bypassing `lower.rs` entirely — structurally unaffected). Dead files `src/vars.rs`/`src/bump_tree.rs` deleted (confirmed zero references repo-wide first; `vars.rs`'s only dependency, `phf`, is still used elsewhere so no `Cargo.toml` change needed). Cargo-level verification BLOCKED at the time by the external wasm4pm-compat issue (separately being fixed this session) — validated via brace-balance check + standalone `rustfmt --check` (zero diff) instead. One useful confirmation from this pass: `wasm4pm_compat::arazzo` (a type this ticket's code depends on) didn't exist on disk in the sibling repo at all at the time — only in its git history — directly corroborating the mid-refactor diagnosis. **Live-verified after the wasm4pm-compat fix**: both new tests (`depends_on_execution_order_resolves_when_declared_out_of_textual_order`, `depends_on_reorder_is_a_no_op_when_no_dependencies_are_declared`) plus the full-pipeline capstone `out_of_textual_order_depends_on_reference_resolves_through_the_real_pipeline` all pass." .

jira:PROJ785
    a jira:Ticket ;
