    jira:evidence "`DIRECT_ACTUATION_REFUSED`, `BROKER_RECEIPT_PRECONDITION_MISSING`, `CORRELATION_MISSING`, `CORRELATION_MISMATCH`, `RETURN_PROVENANCE_MISSING`, `RETURN_AUTHORITY_REFUSED`, `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED`, `RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED` — these are already named in PROJ-758's scope description; this ticket is the one that actually forces each to exist as a distinct tested variant rather than an aspiration inside a bigger ticket. **Updated this session**: 4 of 8 now real via PROJ-757/758 (`DIRECT_ACTUATION_REFUSED`, `CORRELATION_MISSING`) and PROJ-758's remediation (`BROKER_RECEIPT_PRECONDITION_MISSING`, `RETURN_AUTHORITY_REFUSED`) — flagged by PROJ-758's own remediation agent, not silently left stale. Remaining scope: `CORRELATION_MISMATCH`, `RETURN_PROVENANCE_MISSING`, `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED`, `RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED` (4 codes). **Built this session (2 more codes real via a dedicated remediation, 6/8 total).** `CORRELATION_MISMATCH` and `RETURN_PROVENANCE_MISSING` now real, tested checks in `arazzo_runner_broker.erl`, backed by real dispatch-time data (`D#dispatch.correlation_id`/`status`). `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED`/`RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED` correctly left disclosed-unenforced, grep-verified (no output schema exists, no Erlang→praxis-graphlaw bridge exists). **Extended this session (PROJ-810 build wave) — RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED now real too, 7/8 total.** `admit_return_structure/1` (`broker.erl:416`) walks StepDef `outputs` bind-rules to derive `required_result_types`, computed and stored on the ledger at dispatch time (`do_dispatch/6:248`), checked before `admit_return_semantic`. Independently re-verified: both new tests (`arazzo_runner_broker_test.erl:601-693`) are genuinely end-to-end, not tautological — positive test starts a real workflow process and asserts real NIF-executed output; negative test asserts the consequence is refused and the ledger stays `actuated`, never `admitted`. `rebar3 eunit --module=arazzo_runner_broker_test` ×3: 15/15 every run. `RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED` remains correctly BLOCKED — re-investigated fresh, confirmed no output-schema mechanism and no Erlang→praxis-graphlaw SHACL bridge exists (the only `open_port`/`gen_tcp`/`httpc` hits anywhere are test-only AtomVM subprocess spawns, architecturally unrelated). 7 of 8 codes now real. **Built this session (2 of the remaining 4 now real, 2 correctly stayed disclosed-unenforced).** `admit_return/2` → `admit_return/3(DispatchToken, CorrelationId, ReturnerAuthorityToken)`: a known token whose caller-supplied `CorrelationId` doesn't match the ledger's real `D#dispatch.correlation_id` (populated at dispatch time from the workflow identity, not invented) now refuses `CORRELATION_MISMATCH`. New `admit_return_provenance/2` stage checks the real `D#dispatch.status` state-machine field — `dispatched`/`dispatch_failed` (no consequence ever captured via broker-mediated actuation) now refuses `RETURN_PROVENANCE_MISSING`; this closes a gap PROJ-758 had claimed \"trivially satisfied by construction,\" the same overclaim pattern PROJ-758's own remediation found for `required_prior_receipts`. `RETURN_STRUCTURE_REFUSED`/`RETURN_SEMANTIC_REFUSED` correctly left in `?UNENFORCED_RETURN_STAGES` (shrunk from 3 to 2 items) — grep-verified, not assumed: no output schema exists anywhere in `apps/arazzo_runner`/`apps/air_core` to validate structure against, and no NIF/port/httpc bridge exists from Erlang to `crates/praxis-graphlaw` to reach real SHACL/admission semantic validation. `rebar3 eunit --module=arazzo_runner_broker_test`: 13 tests, 0 failures, 7 consecutive runs byte-identical. Full-suite run showed unrelated failures confirmed to belong to a concurrent PROJ-761 agent's own in-flight file, not this change. Now 6/8 codes real, 2/8 honestly disclosed-unenforced." .

