jira:PROJ796
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "796" ;
    jira:title "Wire the Composed Rail A/B Pipeline into `ChatmanEngine::admit_transition`" ;
    jira:section "A/B (`PRD.md:294-370`)" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ750 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ751 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ752 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ753 ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ754 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built and independently verified this session — closes the gap this row previously named.** `ChatmanEngine::admit_transition_with_external_cut` (`crates/praxis-graphlaw/src/chatman/engine.rs:716`) is a real, non-test-only entry point adjacent to `admit_transition` (`engine.rs:616`): it calls `admit_transition` verbatim first, so digests #1-#9 and `receipt_root` stay byte-identical to a plain run (PRD.md sec.19.1 \"local POWL remains local\"), then — only when the caller-supplied `Powl` region declares an `ExternalCut` anywhere (`powl_projection::model_declares_external_cut`) — runs the real Rail A/B pipeline and seals it as a new, disclosed digest #10 (`EngineProcessReceipt::external_cut: Option<Digest>`, deliberately excluded from the existing 9-term `receipt_root` formula so that formula is unchanged). Design decision this ticket had to make: `praxis-graphlaw` cannot depend on `praxis-core` (the reverse edge already exists, so a direct call would be a cyclic crate dependency), so admission depends on a new `ExternalCutCompiler` trait seam (`chatman::powl_projection`) instead, and `praxis_core::arazzo::ChatmanRailAbCompiler` is the one real implementation injected by the caller — `wasm4pm-arazzo`/`powl2-decompose`/`bumpalo` promoted from `[dev-dependencies]` to real `[dependencies]` in `crates/praxis-core/Cargo.toml` accordingly. New production function `ArazzoProjectionReceipt::project_and_compile` (`crates/praxis-core/src/arazzo.rs`) and `ChatmanRailAbCompiler::compile` both call one shared pipeline core (`render_and_compile`), so the sealed engine and a direct crate caller can never diverge — proven, not asserted: `crates/praxis-core/tests/rail_ab_external_cut_wiring.rs`'s content test independently recomputes the engine's private digest-#10 formula over `project_and_compile`'s real output and asserts equality to what `admit_transition_with_external_cut` sealed through the trait, and asserts the manufactured Arazzo document actually contains both declared step kinds. Design decision on failure semantics: a declared cut that fails to compile is a hard refusal of the whole admission (the already-valid S1-S6 transition is discarded), not a soft/partial one. 3 new integration tests (no-cut byte-identical; cut-bearing content verification; determinism across two independent runs) plus a 3x repeated-process determinism check this session (`for i in 1 2 3; do cargo test -p praxis-core --test rail_ab_external_cut_wiring; done` — only build-timing/test-ordering differ in the logs; every digest assertion passed all 3 times). `just praxis-core-test` (111 test-fns across 6 binaries + 1 doctest), `just wasm4pm-arazzo-test` (47 test-fns across 6 binaries — `bench_mmap_vs_read` is a pre-existing timing-comparison test that flaked once under this session's concurrent build load and passed cleanly on an isolated re-run, not a regression), `just powl2-decompose-test` (26 test-fns across 2 binaries) all pass, zero regressions. `just fmt-check-pkg praxis-core` and `praxis-graphlaw` (new scoped recipes, since `just fmt` is workspace-wide) both clean; `cargo clippy -p praxis-core --lib --tests --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean after fixing 2 pre-existing (not authored by this ticket) lints in the same file. Gap, disclosed not hidden: the repo's own `just praxis-graphlaw-check`/`-clippy` and `just praxis-core-clippy` recipes cannot currently run to completion at all — `benches/owlrl.rs` has a pre-existing type error (confirmed via `git log` to predate this session), and `cargo clippy -p praxis-graphlaw --all-targets` has ~52 pre-existing errors and `cargo test -p praxis-graphlaw --lib --tests --no-fail-fast` has 10 pre-existing failing binaries (`knowledge_hooks_e2e_old`/`_tier1-5`, `pattern4_equivalence_canonicalization`, `shacl_sparql_stress`, `shacl_validation`, `shacl_validation_extended`), all confirmed via `git log`/grep to touch zero `chatman/` code and to predate this ticket — a real, out-of-scope repo condition, not this ticket's regression; added `praxis-graphlaw-check-libtests`/`-clippy-libtests` scoped recipes to verify this ticket's own two touched files cleanly (zero clippy findings in `engine.rs`/`powl_projection.rs`, confirmed by direct grep of the clippy log). Second disclosed gap: `ChatmanEngine::verify_replay` does not yet recompute/compare digest #10 (only #1-#9) — external-cut replay-mismatch detection is not yet wired, a named follow-up. **Closed this session — ALIVE, adversarially re-verified.** New `ChatmanEngine::verify_replay_with_external_cut` (`engine.rs`): runs `verify_replay` first (unchanged digests #1-#9), then conditionally recomputes digest #10 via `compile_external_cut_digest` — a single shared helper also used by `admit_transition_with_external_cut`, so the seal and the replay check can never diverge by construction. New `ReplayMismatch::ExternalCut { recorded, replayed }` variant. 2 new tests confirmed present and correct. `just praxis-graphlaw-test-lib 'test(chatman)'`: 154/154, independently re-run. A tampered or drifted manufactured-Arazzo artifact is now caught on replay, closing the gap this row itself named as a follow-up. **Reachability gap closed this session** — `admit_transition_with_external_cut` had exactly 5 call sites, all test-only. New `crates/praxis-core/src/bin/admit-external-cut.rs` (`just admit-external-cut`) is a real, non-test CLI: builds a real `ChatmanEngine`, declares a real `ExternalCut` region (embedded fixture by default, or a real `.ttl` file via `--snapshot`), calls `admit_transition_with_external_cut` through the real `ChatmanRailAbCompiler`, prints all 10 digests and self-checks `recompute_root()`. `grep -rn \"\\.admit_transition_with_external_cut(\"` now shows 6 hits, one genuinely non-test. `just admit-external-cut` run twice (embedded fixture + real file), both exit 0 with a populated digest #10. 71/71 lib tests, 3/3 wiring tests, clippy clean on the new file." .

jira:PROJ797
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "797" ;
    jira:title "Stabilize Rail G Track2b Measurement Output as a Supported External Contract" ;
    jira:section "§16/22 Rail G" ;
    jira:status jira:Planned ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ767 ;
    jira:evidence "The real Track2b measurement (PROJ-767) currently lands at `target/chatman/cng-tests/multifractal/track2b_real/track2b-measurement.txt` — an ephemeral `cargo`-managed path with no receipt discipline, ungoverned by any `just` recipe contract. A real external consumer already exists: mfact's `crates/mo-mae`/`crates/safe-toolbox` have real (non-stub) `compute_renyi_entropy`/`compute_mfp_spectrum_impl` implementations whose tests are gated on `rslab/experiments/praxis_track2b/processed/tick_series.json`, produced by `~/mfact/rslab/scripts/collect_praxis_track2b.py` reading exactly this path — confirmed this session, but the script has never been successfully run end-to-end. Demonstrated fragility, not hypothetical: this exact directory was wiped by an ordinary `cargo clean` earlier in this same session and had to be regenerated. Scope: define a stable, receipted output location/format (or a documented CLI/API surface) for Track2b measurement output, with a `just` recipe that regenerates it deterministically, so an external consumer isn't reading a raw path into `target/`." .

jira:PROJ798
    a jira:Ticket ;
    jira:id "798" ;
    jira:title "Cross-Reference `powl2-decompose` Against `procint`'s Independent Lean Formalization of the Same Source" ;
    jira:section "§7.3 Layer 3 — POWL v2" ;
    jira:status jira:Alive ;
    jira:dependsOn jira:PROJ750 ;
    jira:evidence "**Built this session.** Doc-comment cross-references added to `crates/powl2-decompose/src/powl.rs` only (47 insertions, zero code changes, zero other files touched): module-level pointer to `~/mfact/procint/ProcInt/Models/ChoiceGraph.lean`/`Powl.lean`; `ChoiceGraph`/`GNode` mapped to their Lean counterparts. Found and honestly disclosed, not papered over: a citation discrepancy — this crate's `ChoiceGraph` cites arXiv:2602.15739 Def 3.6 (Kourani/Park/van der Aalst), the Lean file cites a different, earlier paper (arXiv:2505.07052 Def 1) by an overlapping author set; whether these are the same definition restated was NOT verified, said so explicitly. `Powl` (this enum) was deliberately NOT given a clean 1:1 cross-reference — Lean's `Powl.lean` formalizes a different paper entirely (the original tree-structured POWL, BPM 2023), not this crate's graph-based POWL 2.0; asserting equivalence would have been a fabrication. Verification (`just powl2-decompose-test`) was BLOCKED at the time by the wasm4pm-compat issue (root-caused and fixed later this session — see environmental note at end of file). **Live-verified after the fix**: `just powl2-decompose-test` → 19 lib tests + 7 integration tests, 26/26 passing, 0 failed." .

